# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/blob-report/

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# ...except the canonical variable list, which AGENTS.md 8.4 requires to be
# committed. Without this negation `.env*` swallows it, `git add` skips it
# silently, and the list never lands in the repository. Names only, never values.
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# agent skills
# The Drizzle docs snapshot is ~4.5 MB across 484 pages and is regenerable by
# .agents/skills/drizzle-docs/scripts/sync_drizzle_docs.py, so it is not
# tracked — the script and the source stanza next to it are. The Zod snapshot
# is 16 pages / ~292 KB and IS committed, deliberately, so that skill needs no
# setup on a fresh clone.
/.agents/skills/drizzle-docs/references/docs/
/.agents/skills/drizzle-docs/references/docs-index.md
# The Tailwind docs snapshot is ~5 MB across 236 pages and is regenerable by
# .agents/skills/tailwind-4-docs/scripts/sync_tailwind_docs.py, so it is not
# tracked either — but for a second reason on top of size: tailwindcss.com is
# source-available and explicitly NOT open-source, which is why that script
# gates on --accept-docs-license and why the skill ships without the snapshot.
# Committing it here would redistribute it. The script, docs-source.txt,
# engineering-playbook.md and gotchas.md stay tracked; a fresh clone runs the
# sync once.
/.agents/skills/tailwind-4-docs/references/docs/
/.agents/skills/tailwind-4-docs/references/docs-index.tsx
